#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Cuba: Havana, October 1962.  A sample game for the Grognard engine,
and an invasion that never happened.

In October 1962 the United States found Soviet nuclear missiles in Cuba,
and while Kennedy and Khrushchev bargained, the armed forces readied
OPLAN 316: an airborne and amphibious invasion of the island, aimed
first at Havana.  Here the bargaining fails: the Marines land on the
beaches east of the city and two airborne divisions drop on its
airfields.  Nobody in Washington knows that the Soviet regiments
waiting for them have nuclear rockets of their own.  Play either side
against the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./cuba (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is saved
to ~/.cuba.json.  ./cuba --selftest checks the map and plays a game
between two computer players.
"""

